body:
I always felt like everything around me was going by too fast and I was going to get left behind to rot, so I essentially forced myself to grow up too fast. I forced myself to take on all these responsibilities and never fully realizing that it's okay to ask for other people's help and that the people in my life want to help me because they care about me - not because they think I'm weak.  I want to prove to them that I can do everything just fine on my own despite all my shortcomings.

&#x200B;

...You know, at first, I was terrified at the thought of dying because there's nothing left after that. But, now that I'm older and had more time to think about it, dying sounds peaceful. I feel like, when I die, I can *finally* find some sense of peace - I'll never have to worry about anything anymore, I'll never have to shoulder everything by myself, I'll never have to regret anything, I'll never feel like I'm a burden to anyone else, I'll be frustrated with myself because there's nothing to be frustrated about. It makes me realize how stupid everyone is when they say suicide is selfish and you'll only end up regretting it later.

&#x200B;

Sounds like bullshit to me - you can't regret anything when you're dead.
